    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch06-08: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.36";
    dc:description "Existing data permit case studies but not an exhaustive test over all complex organs. The word 'possibly' also makes decisive discrimination unusually difficult.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: For sampled complex organs, reconstruct ancestral states and test whether each transition can be decomposed into small heritable functional changes. One rigorously established organ requiring an inaccessible discontinuity would refute the universal claim, while finite surveys cannot confirm it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Possibility of a pathway is difficult to establish or exclude.", "The universal quantifier cannot be confirmed by sampling.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.7"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch06-08--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch06-08--gpt--dataset-2>;
